  "output": "**I cannot perform this audit: no report is present in this session.**\n\nThe conversation contains no report text, no source list, and no citations to verify. Auditing a document that isn't here would require me to invent both the report and its sources — which is precisely the failure mode you're asking me to check for. Fabricating an audit would be worse than declining to produce one.\n\n**What I would need to proceed:**\n1. The full report text (or the specific claims/sections to audit)\n2. The cited sources, or at minimum enough bibliographic detail (title, author, publication, date, URL/DOI) to locate them\n\n**The audit framework I would apply once the report is supplied:**\n\n*1. Claim–source alignment (no overreach)*\n- For each factual claim, compare the wording against what the source actually states\n- Flag hedging lost in translation (e.g., source says \"may be associated with\" → report says \"causes\")\n- Flag extrapolation beyond the studied population, timeframe, or scope\n- Flag aggregated statistics presented as precise, or single-study findings presented as settled consensus\n\n*2. Contradiction handling*\n- Identify points where sources disagree (differing estimates, contested mechanisms, conflicting dates/figures)\n- Verify the report acknowledges the disagreement rather than silently picking one side\n- Check that any resolution between conflicting sources is justified, not asserted\n- Note whether uncertainty ranges or caveats from the sources were dropped\n\n*3. Citation integrity (no invented references)*\n- Verify every citation corresponds to a real, retrievable publication\n- Confirm each cited work actually supports the claim it's attached to (not just that it exists)\n- Check author names, titles, years, and page/section references against the source\n- Flag any citation that appears plausible but cannot be located — a common hallucination pattern\n\n**Deliverable you'd receive:** a claim-by-claim table with verdicts (Supported / Partially supported / Unsupported / Contradicted), a list of unacknowledged contradictions, a citation verification log, and specific suggested revisions.\n\nIf you paste the report (and its sources or citation list), I will run this audit against them directly.",
